{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>The spirit, etc.</b> These are the words of the prophet, and they are prophecy, like \"and He took of the spirit\" (Numbers 11:25)." "<b>Because YHWH has anointed me.</b> For the prophets are called \"my anointed ones,\" like it: \"Touch not my anointed ones\" (Psalms 105:15), and they are the patriarchs. And Rabbi Moses the Priest said that the answer to \"Because YHWH has anointed me\" is \"I will greatly rejoice in YHWH\" (below, verse 10), but there is no need, for the meaning of יען is \"HaShem has anointed me, to bring good tidings to the afflicted.\"" "<b>Opening of eyes.</b> One word, whose ayin and lamed are doubled, like סחרחר (Psalms 38:11) or ירקרק (Leviticus 13:49), אדמדם [there], and it is a noun."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 61, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:35.769677586Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}